message: "Public Preview. Cite H.A.R.D. Protocol 0.3 with exact protocol 0.3-preview.2, MCP 0.3.0rc2 and Skill/contract 0.3.0-rc.2. The rc.3 DOI identifies only the historical rc.3 release."
type: software
title: "H.A.R.D. Protocol 0.3: Human-centered AI Readiness and Decision Protocol"
authors:
  - family-names: Tak
    given-names: Yejun
version: "0.3-preview.2"
repository-code: "https://github.com/yejuntak/hcai-deployment-readiness"
url: "https://github.com/yejuntak/hcai-deployment-readiness"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: "A Public Preview protocol for reopening consequential decisions in AI-assisted artifacts before bounded engineering commitment. It separates historical rationale from current hypotheses, externalizes relevant system surfaces, records consequential assumptions as first-class revisitable claims, binds assessed challenges to explicit evidence levels, and keeps specified, walkthrough, implemented and runtime-tested evidence separate. Decision compression and implementation outrunning understanding are motivating models, not established causal effects. No controlled empirical validation or deployment approval is claimed."
